accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final type  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  29 removed_month 95 accessioned on  29 removed_month 95 at 09 17 clinical data  35 year old woman with a rapidly growing right breast mass  two years previously  she had a right   excisional biopsy  1  infiltrating ductal carcinoma  95   removed_date cm  grade 3  with focal sarcomatoid metaplasia and focal squamous metaplasia  metaplastic carcinoma   see note  2  ductal carcinoma in situ  5   solid type  adjacent to invasive tumor mass  see note  note  no lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  a moderate quantity of tumor infiltrating lymphocytes are present  the pseudosarcomatous areas have a chondroid appearance and comprise less than 20 per cent of the mass  squamous foci are rare and focally keratinizing  the presence of an adjacent in situ component may indicate that this is an independent primary  the examined inked resection margins appear free of tumor  the frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  estrogen and progesterone receptor stains will be performed on formalin fixed tissue  diagnosis by  john h  eichhorn  m d  signed on  01 removed_month 95 at 15 25                                                                                     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     results of staining of fixed tissue for hormone receptor proteins breast  right   a few tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  a few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  09 removed_month 95 at 10 41 gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast on requisition and confirmed to be right breast by phone with dr  ferguson  is a 6 x 4 x 3cm piece of breast  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a 4 x removed_date x 2cm ill defined  tan pink firm mass within 0 3cm of the inked resection margin  a representative section of the tumor is frozen as fx  1 and kept frozen  six sections of the tumor are submitted in a to f  a section of surrounding breast is submitted in g  resident  saha sadeghi  md     intra operative diagnosis     frozen section diagnosis  1  right breast  metaplastic   matrix producing   carcinoma  o r  resident  chin lee wu  md  phd o r  diagnosis by  ben zion pilch  m d                                                                                  source care unit  same day surgical unit    removed_accession_id  reports to  thomas j lynch  m d  charles mason ferguson  m d  part   breast  right    report_end  , No.
